WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.730
- Well, you were so young
when your father passed.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.040
What memories do you have of him?

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.690
- Yeah, you know, I tell people,

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.030
unfortunately, I only have one.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.110
But it's a special one,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.630
because it's the only one
that I shared with him,

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.000
but none of the other siblings shared.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.769
And that was a little
game that we would play

00:00:16.769 --> 00:00:18.630
when he would come home.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.497
And I would run up into
his arms, and he said,

00:00:20.497 --> 00:00:22.860
"We're gonna play the kissing game today."

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.950
And essentially what that
was is, each one of us

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.690
had a spot on his face.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.880
My brothers on either side of the cheek,

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.796
I was on the forehead, my
sister was off to the side

00:00:32.796 --> 00:00:34.350
of the mouth, and my mom was, of course,

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.003
smack dead in the middle there.

00:00:37.548 --> 00:00:40.080
And he would say, "Okay, where is-",

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.790
and he would just call everybody's name.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.867
My nickname was Bunny,
like the bunny rabbit.

00:00:43.867 --> 00:00:45.360
"Where is Bunny's kiss?"

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.770
I would hit him there,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.440
and he actually would
call them sugar spots.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.797
You know, in the black
community we called them,

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:52.140
"Gimme some sugar."

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.050
So, I gave him some sugar
on each one of those spots

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.640
as he called each person's name.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.790
And that was our little
bonding experience,

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.740
because when I was born, he
started traveling even more.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.250
And so, he wasn't home as
much, and I think he felt

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.240
that he needed to do something special

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.790
so that I would have
that connection with him,

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.820
because my father always had a sense

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.610
that he was not gonna live a long life.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.290
And so, he wanted to make sure

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.860
that there were meaningful
moments with each one of us.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.693
- Well, that's a

00:01:26.693 --> 00:01:30.393
beautiful memory.
(audience clapping)

